    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0374" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 Chiang Kai-shek/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1722</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-22">October 22,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received November 6.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch no.
                    1700 of October 19, 1943, in regard to the inauguration of General Chiang
                    Kai-shek as President of the National Government, I have the honor to enclose a
                    copy of despatch no. 161 of September 29, 1943, from the Secretary on detail at
                    Chengtu regarding the reaction at that city to the acceptance by General Chiang
                    of the presidency.</p>
                <p>Mr. Smith’s despatch, which contains a summary, is of chief interest in that it
                    reveals, as stated in the despatch, the considerable prestige of General Chiang
                    among the people as well as the bitter criticism of some of his close followers.
                    The report mentioned on page 2 of Mr. Smith’s despatch concerning the
                    replacement of the Mayor of Chungking by ex-[<hi rendition="#italic">the
                        late</hi>]President Lin Sen’s chief assistant is not correct; the present
                    Mayor continues to hold his office.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. E. Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d292-a1.xml" xpointer="d292-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
